codex
The wrapper returns `v0`, but it also declares `a0` as an asm output tied to the input, allowing `a0` to be clobbered. That supports one return-register defect; it does not support treating the `a0` write as a second ABI violation. I’m checking for in-tree dependencies on that write and confirming debugger visibility.
